-- title:
--   Base change of automorphisms of a power-series hypersurface
-- statement:
--   Let $W_0$ and $W$ be Noetherian commutative rings and $\psi \colon W_0 \to W$ a ring homomorphism. Let $g_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ and $g \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ be power series in two variables such that the principal ideals $(g)$ and $(\psi_* g_0)$ coincide, where $\psi_*$ denotes `MvPowerSeries.map ψ`, the coefficientwise application of $\psi$. Write $S_0 := W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(g_0)$ and $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(g)$, with quotient maps $\mathrm{mk}_{S_0}$ and $\mathrm{mk}_S$. Suppose given a ring automorphism $\theta_0$ of $S_0$ and a matrix $M_0 \in \mathrm{Mat}_{2\times 2}(W_0)$ such that $\theta_0$ fixes the image of every constant $C(w)$, $w \in W_0$, and such that for each $j \in \{0,1\}$ the difference $\theta_0(\mathrm{mk}_{S_0}(X_j)) - \mathrm{mk}_{S_0}\bigl(\sum_i C((M_0)_{ij}) X_i\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S_0$ generated by $\mathrm{mk}_{S_0}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mk}_{S_0}(X_1)$. Then there exists a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ with three properties: $\theta$ fixes $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$ for every $w \in W$; $\theta$ is compatible with $\theta_0$ along base change, in the sense that whenever $s, s' \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ satisfy $\theta_0(\mathrm{mk}_{S_0}(s)) = \mathrm{mk}_{S_0}(s')$ one has $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(\psi_* s)) = \mathrm{mk}_S(\psi_* s')$; and for each $j$ the difference $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(X_j)) - \mathrm{mk}_S\bigl(\sum_i C(\psi((M_0)_{ij})) X_i\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$.
--
--   This is a piece of commutative algebra about formal power series in two variables: an automorphism of a hypersurface quotient $W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(g_0)$ which is constant on coefficients and has prescribed linear part descends along any homomorphism of Noetherian coefficient rings, retaining both its compatibility with the base-changed quotient map and its linear part. The relational formulation of compatibility, and the generic target ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(g)$ for an arbitrary generator $g$ of the ideal $(\psi_* g_0)$, allow it to be applied directly to the completed local rings of Drinfeld-type charts on modular curves, where it is used in the construction of ring isomorphisms of such completions after base change to an algebraically closed coefficient ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_ringEquiv_quotient_span_comp_map_eq_of_ringEquiv_of_linearPart_of_span_eq.lean

